        "site_admin": false
      },
      "body": "\n\n<details><summary>nit from the Ralph LLM to use monotonic time.</summary>\n\nUse a monotonic clock for the RPC startup deadline (test/functional/test_framework/test_node.py:365, head)\n\ntime.time() can jump during startup polling: a forward adjustment can make the loop fail before rpc_timeout elapses, while a backward adjustment can extend the wait. Use time.monotonic() for both deadline creation and comparison. No actual host-clock adjustment during startup was identified, so the impact is conditional on that trigger.\n\n</details>",
      "created_at": "2026-10-15T08:57:41Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-15T08:57:41Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36439#discussion_r4281013249",
      "pull_request_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/pulls/36439",
      "_links": {
